UPDATE companies SET description='CHUHATSU North America, Inc. operates a 300,000-square-foot facility in Glasgow, Kentucky. The company was formed in February 2017 through the merger of ACK (established 1989) and Chuo Precision Spring, becoming the North American arm of Chuo Spring Co., Ltd., a Japanese spring and control cable manufacturer founded in 1948.

The facility produces a range of automotive springs and control cables, including chassis springs, precision coil springs, flat springs, formed wire springs, leaf springs, torsion bars, torsion springs, snap rings, and spiral springs, as well as heavy-duty and light-duty control cables. Additional capabilities include stamping, e-coating, motor mount assembly, and stabilizer bar production. CHUHATSU serves as both a Tier 1 and Tier 2 supplier to major automobile manufacturers.

Its customer base spans passenger vehicles, commercial vehicles, and ATVs and UTVs, with products designed for automotive OEM and Tier supplier programs from development through long-term production. The company emphasizes custom spring solutions tailored to specific vehicle platforms.

CHUHATSU’s corporate philosophy centers on enriching society through technology, pioneering the future with human wisdom, and challenging itself to fulfill every dream. Its stated objective is to design and manufacture the highest-quality products at competitive prices, provide superior service, meet delivery commitments, and employ qualified people with training opportunities. The company holds ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14001:2015 certifications and has received the President’s Award from its parent company along with multiple customer delivery and performance awards.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Spring coiling and forming", "Stamping", "E-coating", "Control cable assembly", "Motor mount assembly", "Stabilizer bar manufacturing", "Supply chain management", "Customer service"], "industries": ["Automotive OEM", "Tier 1 suppliers", "Tier 2 suppliers", "Passenger vehicles", "Commercial vehicles", "ATVs and UTVs"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tier 1 and Tier 2 supplier to major automobile manufacturers", "300,000+ sq ft state-of-the-art manufacturing facility with adjacent expansion property", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14001:2015 certified", "Global manufacturing footprint across seven countries", "Custom spring solutions from development through long-term production"], "facts_used": ["300,000 sqft facility in Glasgow, KY -> /", "Formed in February 2017 from merger of ACK (1989) and Chuo Precision Spring -> /about", "Parent company Chuo Spring Co. founded December 1948 -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 14001:2015 certified -> /about", "Tier 1 and Tier 2 supplier to major automobile manufacturers -> /about", "Products: chassis springs, precision springs, control cables, flat springs, formed wire springs, leaf springs, torsion bars, torsion springs, snap rings, spiral springs, stabilizer bars, motor mounts, e-coat, stamping -> /", "Industries: passenger vehicles, commercial vehicles, ATVs & UTVs -> /", "Corporate philosophy and objective -> /about", "President''s Award from parent company -> /about", "Global facilities in 7 countries -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CHUHATSU North America, Inc. is a 300,000 sqft facility in Glasgow, KY.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='chuhatsu-north-america-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='CM Solutions, Inc. was founded in 2002 in Corinth, Mississippi, as a privately owned contract manufacturer serving all electronics market segments. The company was established by Mike, Ron, Jack, and Tommy, who brought decades of combined experience in OEM and contract manufacturing both domestically and abroad. The founders remain actively involved in daily operations, maintaining a hands-on approach with customers.

The firm provides end-to-end electronic manufacturing services (EMS), including build-to-order (BTO), configure-to-order (CTO), and direct-ship programs that integrate seamlessly into customer supply chains. Over its history, CM Solutions has expanded its facility three times, growing to five production lines equipped with selective soldering, automatic optical inspection (AOI), multiple in-circuit test platforms, a DEK Horizon SMT printer, a Faraday cage for RF circuitry, and a dedicated conformal coating room. The company supports low-, medium-, and high-volume production with lead-free (RoHS-compliant) processes.

CM Solutions serves a range of industries, including automotive, medical, military, and general OEM markets. Its customer base spans domestic and international clients seeking customized manufacturing solutions for electronic assemblies. The company’s quality system aligns with IPC-A-610 Classes 1–3 and J-STD-001 standards, enabling it to meet the stringent requirements of regulated sectors.

