UPDATE companies SET description='CVC Metal Fabricating operates from Florence, Kentucky, in the Greater Cincinnati region. The company traces its roots to the Cincinnati Ventilating Co. Inc., established more than 80 years ago, and has remained a family-owned-and-operated business across four generations.

The shop specializes in metal fabrication, producing component parts, assemblies, and complete products. Its capabilities include six-axis laser cutting, nine-axis forming, robotic welding, and multiple flexible manufacturing systems, allowing it to handle a range of project sizes.

CVC serves customers from small businesses to large corporations, primarily across the Greater Cincinnati metropolitan area but also nationwide. The company does not publicly list specific industry verticals, focusing instead on general metal fabrication needs.

The company emphasizes technology-driven manufacturing, investing in cutting-edge equipment to deliver quality and consistency at competitive prices. Its stated mission is to provide quality products in a timely manner using high-tech equipment, backed by ISO 9001:2008 certification and a commitment to superior service and dedication.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Metal fabrication", "Six-axis laser cutting", "Nine-axis forming", "Robotic welding", "Flexible manufacturing systems"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Six-axis laser cutting", "Nine-axis forming", "Robotic welding", "Flexible manufacturing systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Six-axis laser cutting", "Nine-axis forming", "Robotic welding", "Multiple flexible manufacturing systems", "ISO 9001:2008 certified"], "facts_used": ["Company name: CVC Metal Fabricating -> db", "Headquarters: Florence, Kentucky -> db", "Founded as Cincinnati Ventilating Co. Inc. over 80 years ago -> /", "Family-owned across four generations -> /", "ISO 9001:2008 certified -> /", "Capabilities: six-axis laser cutting, nine-axis forming, robotic welding, flexible manufacturing systems -> /", "Serves small businesses to large corporations, Greater Cincinnati and nationwide -> /", "Mission: provide quality product timely using high-tech equipment -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Today, we are an industry leader in the fabrication of component parts, assemblies, and complete products.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cvc-metal-fabricating' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cable Conveyor Systems Inc. was founded in 1975 in Columbia, South Carolina. President David M. Rauscher has been with the company since its inception and leads the business alongside Vice President Brooke Spence.

The company designs, manufactures, and installs custom cable conveyor systems for processors that move cans or plastic containers. Its product line includes cable can tracks, diverter gates, accessories, reconditioning parts, and bulk can cable, all built in aluminum or stainless steel. Cable Conveyor holds several national and international patents for its equipment, notably the Extruda-Mold® cable splicing system. Services span consulting, system design, on-site audits, and a portable splicing service that can be performed at a customer’s plant in about one hour.

Primary markets are food, dairy, beverage, motor oil, laundry soap, and pet food manufacturers—any operation that conveys cans or plastic containers. Customers range from new installations to existing lines needing integration, flow improvements, or production increases.

The firm emphasizes a full-service model: on-site audits deliver a photo‑documented report with a flat fee plus travel, and its patented Extruda-Mold splicing technique is guaranteed for two years on full can lines and four years on empty can lines. The stated mission is to provide excellent customer service through customized solutions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom conveyor system design and build", "Conveyor system integration into existing lines", "Extruda-Mold\u00ae cable splicing service", "Extruda-Mold\u00ae splicing machine rental and sales", "On-site system audits", "Reconditioning of conveyor parts", "Consulting for conveying solutions", "Cable can track manufacturing", "Diverter gate manufacturing", "Can cable supply (various styles)", "Accessory and replacement parts fabrication"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Dairy", "Beverage", "Motor oil", "Laundry soap", "Pet food", "Manufacturers using cans or plastic containers"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Stainless steel", "Steel", "Poly-tire coating"], "equipment": ["Extruda-Mold\u00ae Cable Splicing Machines", "Cable Can Tracks", "Diverter Gates", "Extruda-Mold\u00ae Splicer"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented Extruda-Mold\u00ae cable splicing technique", "Splicing completed in one hour, guaranteed 2 years (full cans) / 4 years (empty cans)", "On-site audit service with flat fee plus travel expenses", "Full-service: consulting, design, customization, and implementation of conveying systems", "Multiple national and international patents on conveyor equipment"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 in Columbia, SC -> db", "President David M. Rauscher involved from beginning -> /about", "VP Brooke Spence -> /about", "Manufactures conveying systems for cans/plastic containers -> /", "Industries: food, dairy, beverage, motor oil, laundry soap, pet food -> /", "Products: cable can tracks, diverter gates, accessories, reconditioning parts, can