UPDATE companies SET description='CableLabs operates from Louisville, Colorado, where it was founded in 1988 as a non-profit research and development consortium funded by the global cable industry.

The lab conducts research and development across state-of-the-art facilities, develops industry specifications (including DOCSIS standards), manages patents and licensing, and fosters collaboration among cable operators, equipment manufacturers, and technology providers. Through its subsidiary Kyrio, CableLabs operates a testing and certification operation with more than 180 test benches, 175 equipment racks, and over $120 million in invested infrastructure, having certified more than 1,500 products to date. The organization holds over 800 granted patents spanning three decades.

CableLabs serves the broadband telecommunications sector, working directly with over 2,250 vendor companies and 22,000 individual members across the cable industry ecosystem. Its technologies underpin more than 550 million shipped devices based on its cable modem specifications, and its standards influence a $460 billion industry reaching over half a billion users daily.

The consortium was established to advance connectivity technologies for the benefit of the cable industry, focusing on secure delivery of high-speed data, video, voice, and next-generation services. By aligning government and industry priorities through technology policy work, CableLabs aims to promote innovation, facilitate trade, and strengthen competitiveness across the broadband landscape.', certifications=ARRAY['501(c)(6) non-profit status','National Cooperative Research and Production Act (NCRPA) approved']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Research and Development", "Specifications and Standards Development", "Industry Collaboration", "Strategic Consulting", "Patents & Licensing", "Testing and Certification (via Kyrio)", "Security Services", "Software Solutions", "Differentiated Services", "Network as a Service", "Context-aware Services", "Secure Federated API-enabled Services"], "industries": ["Cable telecommunications", "Broadband technology", "Telecommunications equipment manufacturing", "Network technology standards"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "550+ million devices shipped using CableLabs specifications", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Non-profit R&D consortium funded by global cable industry members", "Develops and maintains industry specifications (DOCSIS, OpenOMCI, etc.)", "Operates Kyrio subsidiary with 180+ test benches for certification testing", "Holds 800+ granted patents over 30+ years", "Technologies deployed in 550+ million devices worldwide"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> /about", "Headquartered in Louisville, Colorado -> db", "Non-profit 501(c)(6) funded by cable industry members -> /about", "Operates under NCRPA -> /about", "CEO Phil McKinney -> /about", "Board includes executives from Comcast, Charter, Cox, etc. -> /about", "Kyrio subsidiary with 180+ test benches, 175 racks, $120M investment -> description and /about", "1,500+ certified products -> /about", "800+ granted patents over 30+ years -> /about", "2,250+ vendor companies engaged -> /about", "550+ million devices shipped based on cable modem spec -> /about", "22,000+ active individual members -> /about", "$460 billion industry influenced -> /about", "Develops DOCSIS specifications -> /about and /", "Provides testing, certification, technical leadership -> /about"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "CableLabs is funded by its cable industry member companies as a non-profit Innovation and R&D lab under Internal Revenue Code 501(c)(6) status.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cablelabs' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cadence, Inc. is headquartered in DeLand, Florida. The company operates as a contract manufacturer specializing in medical devices and precision components for the MedTech and pharmaceutical industries.

Cadence provides vertically integrated contract manufacturing from complex components to finished devices. Its core capabilities include custom sharps (specialty blades and needles), plastics overmolding, insert molding, and injection molding; complex machining such as Swiss, screw, micro, PEEK, and LaserSwiss; precision metal stamping with microstamping, multi-slide, and reel-to-reel technology; deep draw forming; metal injection molding (MIM); and precision laser processing (welding, cutting, marking, drilling, ablation). The company runs certified ISO Class 7 and Class 8 cleanrooms at dedicated facilities in Cranberry Township, Pennsylvania, and Alajuela, Costa Rica, and operates FDA-registered, cGMP-compliant sites in Pennsylvania, Virginia, Costa Rica, Rhode Island, and Wisconsin. It also designs and builds custom automation equipment for assembly and inspection.

Cadence serves MedTech and Pharma original equipment manufacturers worldwide, supporting applications in medical devices, drug delivery systems, and diagnostics. Customers range from large multinational OEMs to early-stage innovators requiring design for manufacturability (DFM), design for assembly (DFA), prototyping, process validation (IQ/OQ/PQ), and new product introduction (NPI) support.

The company emphasizes a single-source model that consolidates the supply chain, reduces time to market, and leverages external expertise. A dedicated sterilization management facility and comprehensive quality system (ISO 13485:2016, FDA 21 CFR Part 820) are cited as key differentiators for ensuring compliance and patient safety.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','FDA 21 CFR Part 820','cGMP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Finished device assembly and packaging", "Certified cleanroom manufacturing (ISO Class 7, ISO Class 8)", "Custom automation design and integration", "Custom sharps manufacturing (specialty blades and needles)", "Plastics overmolding", "Insert molding", "Injection molding", "Complex machining (Swiss, screw, micro, PEEK, LaserSwiss)", "Precision metal stamping (microstamping, multi-slide, reel-to-reel, in-house die design)", "Deep draw forming", "Metal injection molding (MIM)", "Precision laser processing (welding, cutting, marking, drilling, ablation)", "Product and process development (DFM, DFA, prototyping, validation, NPI)", "Supply chain management", "Sterilization management", "Quality management system (ISO 13485:2016)", "Regulatory compliance (FDA 21 CFR Part 820, cGMP)"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Pharmaceuticals", "Drug Delivery", "Diagnostics", "MedTech"], "materials": ["PEEK"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in DeLand, Florida -> db", "ISO 13485:2016 certification -> /quality", "FDA 21 CFR Part 820 registered facilities in PA, VA, Costa Rica, RI, WI -> /services", "cGMP compliance -> /services", "Cleanroom facilities in Cranberry Township, PA (ISO Class 7) and Alajuela, Costa Rica (ISO Class 7) -> /capabilities", "Custom sharps manufacturing (specialty blades and needles) -> /capabilities", "Plastics overmolding, insert molding, injection molding -> /capabilities", "Complex machining: Swiss, screw, micro, PEEK, LaserSwiss -> /capabilitie