UPDATE companies SET description='Classic Metal Craft, Inc. has operated from St. Louis, Missouri since 1989. It began as a specialist in ornamental ironwork, building a reputation for quality workmanship and customer satisfaction over more than three decades.

The firm produces custom ornamental ironwork ranging from standard wrought-iron fencing and handrails to hand-forged decorative pieces. Its in-house capabilities include custom fabrication of balconies, juliet balconies, drive gates, portico entrance gates, farm entrance gates, spiral stairs, custom table bases, and integrated exterior lighting. A showroom and production facility at 1315 S. Vandeventer houses experienced craftsmen who handle welding, forging, laser cutting, and CAD-based design visualization.

Classic Metal Craft serves residential homeowners, architects, and commercial contractors throughout the St. Louis region. Recent projects include a modern drive gate for a Clayton home, a farm entrance gate matching an existing wood fence, a six-foot-diameter spiral stair with laser-cut treads for a West County residence, and a custom iron table base supporting a 250-pound solid wood top in a kitchenette. The company also works on commercial installations, providing CAD drawings for project visualization.

The Zadrozinski family emphasizes employee loyalty and continuous investment in technology as differentiators. Craftsmen often stay with the company for years, and the firm uses CAD to bring client visions to reality before fabrication begins. Quality and craftsmanship are cited as the hallmarks of its success, with a focus on matching existing architectural details and meeting strict design constraints such as maximum opening sizes for pet safety.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom ornamental iron fabrication", "Wrought iron fencing and handrails", "Hand forging", "Welding", "Laser cutting", "CAD design and visualization", "Installation services", "Custom balcony and stair fabrication", "Custom gate fabrication (drive, entrance, farm)", "Custom table base fabrication", "Exterior lighting integration", "Design consultation"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Architectural metalwork", "Home renovation", "Landscape architecture"], "materials": ["Steel", "Wrought iron"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1989", "In-house custom fabrication of all ornamental ironwork", "CAD design for accurate project visualization", "Long-tenured craftsmen with deep experience", "Combined showroom and production facility in St. Louis"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 -> db", "Family-owned by Zadrozinski family -> db", "Headquarters St. Louis, Missouri -> db", "Peter Zadrozinski named as contact -> /", "Offers standard wrought-iron fencing and handrails to custom hand-forged decorative ironwork -> /", "Showroom and production facility at 1315 S. Vandeventer -> /", "Experienced craftsmen with long tenure -> /", "Custom fabrication of balconies, juliet balconies, drive gates, portico entrance gates, farm entrance gates, spiral stairs, table bases, exterior lighting -> /", "CAD design for project visualization -> /", "Residential projects in Clayton, Lafayette Square, West County -> /", "Commercial projects mentioned -> /", "Employee loyalty and investment in technology emphasized -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "CMC offers everything from standard wrought-iron fencing and handrails to custom designed hand-forged decorative ironwork.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='classic-metal-craft' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Classic Metal LLC operates from Pearl, Mississippi, where it was founded in 1999 as Copper Creations by Wade Usey. The business began in a garage, with Usey self-teaching metal fabrication to supply roofing products that were otherwise unavailable locally. His wife Jackie assisted on a metal brake while he installed pieces on job sites. In 2022 the company rebranded to Classic Metal and formalized its structure, now led by the father‑son team of Wade and Reid Usey.

The shop produces custom metal roofing components including roof flashing, chimney caps, conductor heads, finials, standing seam panels, vents, awnings, and chimney crickets.

Primary customers are residential roofers, new‑construction builders, gutter companies, and individual homeowners across the local region. The company also supplies roofing contractors and has begun targeting broader markets in neighboring states. Long‑standing relationships with area builders date back to the founder’s early roofing career.

