UPDATE companies SET description='Cooper Steel Fabricators Inc operates from its headquarters in Shelbyville, Tennessee, with additional fabrication facilities in Childersburg, Alabama, and Monroe, Virginia. The company was founded in 1960 and has remained a family-owned and operated business for over six decades.

The firm specializes in structural steel fabrication and erection, offering preconstruction, project management, field operations, and self-perform erection services. Its three fabrication shops provide more than 385,000 square feet of operational space, and the company ranks among the top 15 purchasers of mill-produced steel in the United States. Capabilities include robotic fabrication, plate girder and truss production, oversized assemblies, specialty coatings, and BIM-enabled detailing and connection design.

Cooper Steel serves sectors such as manufacturing, distribution, aerospace, commercial, food and beverage, and mission-critical infrastructure. Its project portfolio includes major distribution facilities and mission-critical structures for national companies. The company''s 24/7 project management teams and in-house erection crews with dedicated safety personnel and certified welding inspectors differentiate it from fabricators that subcontract erection.

The company''s founding principle—“Give Big, Expect Little”—reflects a culture that prioritizes relationships and community. A safety program recognized with multiple AISC and SEAA awards, including Erector Safety Award of Honor honors across several years, underscores its commitment to workforce well-being alongside on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['SEAA World Class Fabricator Safety Excellence (2026)','SEAA Safety Accommodation Award (2025)','AISC Erector Safety Commendation (2015, 2016, 2017, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025)','AISC Fabricator Safety Commendation (2022, 2024, 2025)','SEAA Safety Excellence Premier Award (2023)','AISC Erector Safety Award of Honor (2012, 2013, 2014, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020, 2023)','SEAA World Class Erector Safety Excellence Award (2021)','AISC Fabricator Safety Award of Honor (2014, 2015, 2016, 2017, 2018, 2020)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Steel erection", "Preconstruction services", "Project management", "Field operations", "Robotic fabrication", "Plate girder fabrication", "Truss fabrication", "Oversized assembly fabrication", "Paint, galvanizing, and specialty coatings", "Intumescent coatings", "BIM coordination", "Detailing, engineering, and connection design", "Barcode tracking", "Shipping and logistics", "Material procurement", "Quality control", "Safety management", "Self-perform erection", "Value engineering", "Design-build", "Constructability reviews", "Schedule development and sequencing", "Logistics planning"], "industries": ["Manufacturing", "Distribution", "Aerospace", "Commercial", "Advanced Industries", "Advanced Technology", "Aviation", "Distribution & E-Commerce", "Food & Beverage", "Industrial & Manufacturing", "Mission Critical"], "materials": ["Structural steel", "Mill-produced steel"], "equipment": ["Robotic fabrication systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Self-perform erection with in-house crews, dedicated safety personnel, and certified welding inspectors", "Top 15 U.S. purchaser of mill-produced steel", "385,000+ square feet of fabrication capacity across three Southeast facilities", "24/7 multi-tiered project management teams", "Robotic fabrication and advanced technology integration"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1960 -> /", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Headquarters in Shelbyville, Tennessee -> /about-us", "Fabrication facilities in Shelbyville TN, Childersburg AL, Monroe VA -> /about-us", "385,000+ sq ft fabrication space -> /services", "Top 15 purchaser of mill-produced steel -> /services", "Services: preconstruction, project management, fabrication, field operations, erection -> /services", "Robotic fabrication with advanced technologies -> /services", "Plate girder, trusses, oversized assemblies -> /services", "Paint, galvanizing, specialty coatings including intumescent -> /services", "BIM coordination, detailing, engineering, connection design -> /services", "Barcode tracking, shipping & logistics -> /services", "24/7 project management teams -> /services", "Self-perform erection with dedicated safety personnel and CWI -> /services", "Industries served: manufacturing, distribution, aerospace, commercial, advanced industries, advanced technology, aviation, distribution & e-commerce, food & beverage, industrial & manufacturing, mission critical -> /, /services", "Safety awards: SEAA and AISC recognitions across multiple years -> /services", "Leadership team names and titles -> /about-us", "Core value: Give Big, Expect Little -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Cooper Steel is a national leader in structural steel fabrication and erection.", "founded_year": "1960", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cooper-steel-fabricators-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Corporate Images Inc., operating as Embroidery By Design, has managed event merchandise and brand activation programs from its Denver, Colorado facility since 1979. The company was founded as a managed apparel and branded merchandise partner, providing in-house decoration and fulfillment services.

The company provides end-to-end uniform and apparel programs, event merchandise, and brand activation services. All production occurs under one roof: embroidery, screen printing, direct-to-film (DTF) printing, kitting, and fulfillment. With a staff of 50, Corporate Images manages inventory, operates client ordering portals, handles budget reporting, and provides customer service. The firm handles high-volume projects such as gate giveaways of 25,000+ shirts for events with up to 39,000 attendees, and daily drop-ship fulfillment for a national retailer with 2,500 locations.

Clients span transportation and fleet, hospitality and restaurant, enterprise retail, sports and events, healthcare, field services, and corporate sectors. Examples include a national carrier with 3,400 drivers across 22 states using a centralized ordering portal, a regional restaurant group with 200 employees across 14 locations, and a national retailer with 2,500 locations receiving daily drop-ship fulfillment.

